From 11e2267598be5ab59b84a1fe1334be02894c6132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] perf(sim): B2 G2 kernels: resumable access searches,
 NIMBY run, police need run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shared pieces the split services pass builds on (docs/dev/B2_DESIGN.md §4).
Whole-call functions keep their code and semantics; results are unchanged.

- catchments: RoadTimeRun (roadTimeMulti: the seed scan by cell ranges, the
  drain with the budget checked before an entry is taken) and RoadDistRun
  (roadDistMulti, 8 circular buckets), each on a private queue (other code
  calls reachRaw / roadDistMulti on the module engine between pieces); the
  bucket being drained is detached first, so a resumed drain pops the whole
  call's sequence. TierProvider.needRun / TierNeedRun: a provider's need
  raster as a resumable run.
- transit: transitCoverageRange (the disks of a stop range, not cleared);
  computeTransitCoverage = fill + one range.
- nimby: NimbyRun replaces the module scratch (one run per owner; pre-B2 two
  cities in one process shared it): fills, building chunks (splatAdd sums in
  list order), landfill row pairs, corridor ranges on multiples of 4 (the
  word skip runs as in the whole rebuild), the final pass by rows into
  private rasters, a publish piece (.set + the cost estimate).
  rebuildNimby / nimbyCost keep their semantics (the J4 frozen-original test
  passes: rebuildNimby = the run with nothing in between).
- facilities: the police need as a run (review 2 item 5b): the monthly scan
  in chunks over the pass list (installed with the list's nextBuildingId),
  the job sites in chunks (same compaction), the cell pass by ranges.
  monthlyScan = the same parts in one go.
- traffic: attachRefreshMs(st), the estimate of a pending lazy attachment
  refresh, so other tasks can run it in a piece of their own (review 2
  item 5e).

